{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":587,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:2Kgs.15","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"2 Kings","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"2 Kings 15","reference":"2 Kings 15","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"The reign of Azariah, ver."},{"verse":2,"text":"1-7."},{"verse":3,"text":"Of Zachariah, ver."},{"verse":4,"text":"8-12."},{"verse":5,"text":"Of Shallum, ver."},{"verse":6,"text":"13-15."},{"verse":7,"text":"Of Menahem, ver."},{"verse":8,"text":"16-22."},{"verse":9,"text":"Of Pekahiah, ver."},{"verse":10,"text":"23-26."},{"verse":11,"text":"Of Pekah, ver."},{"verse":12,"text":"27-31."},{"verse":13,"text":"Of Jotham, ver."},{"verse":14,"text":"32-38."},{"verse":15,"text":"1.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":16,"text":"To reign - Solely and fully to exercise his regal power.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":17,"text":"5.","scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":18,"text":"A leper - The cause whereof see 2 Chron. xxvi, 16.","scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":19,"text":"8.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":20,"text":"Six months - After the throne had been vacant several years, thro' the dissentions that were in the kingdom.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":21,"text":"13.","scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":22,"text":"Full moon - That dominion seldom lasts long, which is founded in blood and falsehood.","scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":23,"text":"30.","scriptureVerseStart":30,"scriptureVerseEnd":30},{"verse":24,"text":"Twentieth year - The meaning is, that he began his reign in the twentieth year after the beginning of Jotham's reign; or, which is the same thing, in the fourth year of Ahaz, son of Jotham.","scriptureVerseStart":30,"scriptureVerseEnd":30},{"verse":25,"text":"33.","scriptureVerseStart":33,"scriptureVerseEnd":33},{"verse":26,"text":"To reign - Alone: for he had reigned before this, as his father's deputy.","scriptureVerseStart":33,"scriptureVerseEnd":33},{"verse":27,"text":"35.","scriptureVerseStart":35,"scriptureVerseEnd":35},{"verse":28,"text":"Gate - Not of the temple, but of one of the courts of the temple, probably that which led to the king's palace.","scriptureVerseStart":35,"scriptureVerseEnd":35}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"2 Kings","chapter":15}}